 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R15 (block 263000) -- PROSECUTION THROUGH THE CORRUPTIBLE COUNCIL (R9 / 247). bv_prosecute files a proven case with the council; bv_council_convict / bv_council_acquit adjudicate over the backing-graph (Sum of vote over SEATED CouncilMembers > 0 -> a Conviction) -- John's seat is a bloc that can BLOCK a true prosecution (vote=-1) or PUSH a false one (vote=+1); ablate his seat (is_seated=0) and the outcome flips (a clean structural counterfactual). bv_warn / bv_punish sanction by AMOUNT magnitude (warn if amount<=warn_threshold else punish) -- magnitude, not the trigger, sets the severity. A Sanction is a graph record (censure), NOT a reward/punishment token on a person. ZERO new Rust.",
